    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1314">

                <pb facs="1408" n="1394" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.415/6–2944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stewart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-30T19:00:00-04:00">June 30, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>288. The Department feels that in view of the internal political situation in
                        Nicaragua<anchor n="5" xml:id="d1314-f1"/> it would not be advisable for
                    President <pb facs="1409" n="1395" xml:id="pg1395"/> Somoza to use the Embassy
                    balcony as a rostrum on July 4, as mentioned in your 400 of June 29, 6 p.m. You
                    should find some discreet way of bringing about the abandonment of this part of
                    his plans. The Embassy’s attitude toward the manifestation should be one of
                    cordial but circumspect cooperation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1314-f1" n="5" xml:id="d1314-f1-content">
                <p>Reference is to an outbreak of political disturbances on June 27.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
